    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1550">

                <pb facs="0993" n="877" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg877"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.51/77.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul General Hanna to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate General</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Monterey</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-31T13:00:00-06:41">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 31, 1914, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to case of French priests at Zacatecas: Secretary Foreign Relations
                    Fabela just stated at Consulate this morning that Carranza had official report
                    that no French priests were killed or imprisoned at Zacatecas but that they were
                    deported from the country.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
